course: dictionary
lesson: 7203
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word pew is a good example. In church, a pew is a long wooden bench with a back, where people sit. «Noah kicked the pew all through the sermon (the priest's long talk).» The words church and sermon tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. In British speech, «Take a pew» is a friendly, informal way to say «sit down», so pew can also mean a seat. When someone says «Pew! What stinks?», it is not a bench at all. It is a sound people make at a bad smell.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Noah kicked the bench» fit a church talk? Yes, a pew is a bench in a church. Does «Pew! What stinks?» need a bench? No, so here pew is a sound.
fact: A pew is a long wooden bench with a back, where people sit in a church.
fact: The front pews in a church are often for the family at a wedding or funeral.
fact: «Take a pew» is an informal way of saying «sit down».
fact: «Pew!» or «pee-yew!» is a sound people make when something smells very bad.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always read the words around it.
exercise: What is a pew, in a church? | *A long wooden bench with a back | A small table for candles | A tall tower with a bell | A kind of stained glass window
exercise: Aunt Ruth says «Take a pew» when you walk in. What does she mean? | Leave the room | Open the window | Go to bed | *Sit down
exercise: Your friend holds her nose and says «Pew! What stinks?» What is pew here? | A friendly hello | A long wooden bench | *A sound people make at a bad smell | A kind of church window
test: «The building helps too: the font for baptism, the pulpit for preaching, the lectern for reading, the altar or communion table, the pews, and often stained glass.» Which of these is a place where people sit? | The font | The altar | The pulpit | *The pews
test: Lucy says «Pew!» as she walks past the bins. What is she telling you? | Lucy is singing in church | Lucy is sad | Lucy wants a seat | *The bins smell very bad
exam: «The front pew was full of flowers for the wedding.» What is a pew in this sentence? | *A long wooden bench in a church | A flower | A bell | A wedding dress
